  "description": "Takes the keystone residual-frontier step: the lambda-COLORED Sigma(2,3,5)=S^3/2I WRT invariant (the bare probe keystone_habiro_wrt_s3_2i computed only the closed-manifold number and pinpointed 'colored insertions' as the open step). Coloring the order-5 icosahedral fibre by SU(2) colour alpha shifts the Lawrence-Zagier false-theta support 30(1+-1/2+-1/3+-1/5) -> 30(1+-1/2+-1/3+-alpha/5). alpha=1 reproduces the bare {1,11,19,29}; alpha=2 gives the complementary E8 exponents {7,13,17,23}; the two lowest colours generate ALL EIGHT E8 exponents {1,7,11,13,17,19,23,29}. So the colored insertions lift the bare single invariant to the E8-exponent-indexed FAMILY that must carry the W_lambda = bwS0^2 resolution. Computes Psi^(alpha)(1/q0) for alpha=1..4 and the n=5 d_q/bwS0 values. No fit; direct Psi=W_lambda not asserted (type-correct structural deliverable: the colored family exists and is E8-indexed).",
